---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const gh = "https://github.com/leat-consulting";
---

<Base
  title="Demo"
  description="The public repositories behind Leat Consulting: reusable workflows, the governance that protects them, and the pull requests that built them."
>
  <section class="band band--hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Demo</span>
    <h1>Everything here is real and public</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      These repositories build and protect this website, and every change to them arrived through a reviewed
      pull request. Read the code, the rules and the history.
    </p>
  </section>

  <ul class="grid-2">
    <li class="card">
      <h2><a href={`${gh}/platform-workflows`}>platform-workflows</a></h2>
      <p>
        The reusable workflows: CI, security scanning, multi-architecture container builds with verified
        provenance, and verified GitHub Pages deploys. A self-test runs every workflow on each change, and
        scans a branch of planted problems to prove each scanner still catches them.
      </p>
      <ul class="ticks small">
        <li><a href={`${gh}/platform-workflows/pull/1`}>Pull request 1</a>: organisation governance as code, written by our Claude GitHub App and merged only after a person approved it.</li>
        <li><a href={`${gh}/platform-workflows/pull/2`}>Pull request 2</a>: the first workflows. Its first run failed on a GitHub permissions rule, and the fix is in the history.</li>
        <li><a href={`${gh}/platform-workflows/releases/tag/v1.0.0`}>Release v1.0.0</a>: an immutable release that callers pin by commit.</li>
        <li><a href={`${gh}/platform-workflows/tree/main/governance`}>governance</a>: the rules and settings, with a drift check and evidence that they bind even the owner.</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li class="card">
      <h2><a href={`${gh}/leat-site`}>leat-site</a></h2>
      <p>
        The source for this website. It calls the shared workflows for CI, scanning and deployment, and each
        deploy is signed and verified before it goes live.
      </p>
      <ul class="ticks small">
        <li><a href={`${gh}/leat-site/blob/main/.github/workflows/pr.yml`}>Pull request checks</a>: build, tests, security scan and a Lighthouse quality check.</li>
        <li><a href={`${gh}/leat-site/blob/main/.github/workflows/main.yml`}>Deploy</a>: built once, signed, verified and deployed from main.</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li class="card">
      <span><span class="badge">Planned</span></span>
      <h2><a href={`${gh}/demo-app`}>demo-app</a></h2>
      <p>
        A small service that will show the whole flow on an application: AI review catching a bug, an AI fix
        approved by a person, a change blocked by a security scan, and a container image checked before it runs.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</Base>
